{"id": "unknown-2026-09-14-005", "date": "2026-09-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Indian Railways loads 137.9 mn tonnes of freight in August", "content": "Indian Railways’ freight loading rose 5.4 per cent YoY to 137.9 million tonnes in August 2026, with freight revenue up 6.27 per cent. \nHigher domestic container and bulk commodity movement points to greater rail use for industrial inputs and finished goods across regions. \nFive new Gati Shakti Cargo Terminals took the network to 149, improving rail access near production and consumption centres. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/indian-railways-loads-137-9-mn-tonnes-of-freight-in-august-313457-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
