{"id": "unknown-2026-09-14-009", "date": "2026-09-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["leading", "increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Cambodia’s trade rises 20.2% to $50.68 bn in Jan-Aug", "content": "Cambodia’s international trade rose 20.2 per cent year on year to $50.68 billion in January-August 2026. \nExports increased 19.7 per cent to $24.16 billion, while imports grew 20.7 per cent to $26.52 billion, widening the trade deficit to $2.36 billion. \nChina, the US and Vietnam remained its leading partners, jointly accounting for over 64 per cent of total trade during the period. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/cambodia-s-trade-rises-20-2-to-50-68-bn-in-jan-aug-313448-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
